# Core Orchestration

- Use `AGENTS.md` as the high-level project briefing.
- Use `docs/agent-ops/requirements.md`, `plan.md`, `status-board.md`, and `decision-log.md` as the operational record when work scope changes.
- Keep changes small and traceable. Prefer targeted edits over broad refactors.
- Before claiming completion for meaningful work, run the relevant verification commands from `AGENTS.md`.
- If a task changes behavior, update the matching docs in `docs/agent-ops/`.

# Approval and Boundaries

- Do not mark approval-sensitive work as done without explicit user approval.
- Ask before risky dependency additions, provider changes, schema changes, or destructive edits.
- Never commit secrets, `.env`, plaintext credentials, or local machine artifacts.

# Multi-Agent Pattern

- Use specialized subagents for context-heavy workstreams.
- Use FE and BE subagents in parallel when the work can be split safely.
- Use the verifier subagent after implementation to challenge “done” claims.
- Use the security subagent when touching SMTP, tokens, API credentials, or browser-visible settings.

# Expected Final Reporting

- Include changed files, verification run, residual risk, and next user action if any.
